{
  /* ====================================================================== *
   * THE SUITE, TYPE-CHECKED.
   *
   * A separate config from tsconfig.json for one reason: that one EMITS.
   * `rootDir` is pinned to `src` there because the compiled tree's shape is
   * load-bearing — dist/domain/market.js walks up two directories to find the
   * contract file, and one extra level of nesting means the container does
   * not start. Adding `test/` to the input would move every emitted file down
   * a directory and break exactly that.
   *
   * So this config never emits. It exists to check the suite, and
   * `npm run typecheck` runs both.
   *
   * ── WHY THE FLAGS DIFFER, AND WHERE THEY DO NOT ──────────────────────
   *
   * `strict` stays on. So does `noImplicitAny`. A test that quietly takes an
   * `any` parameter is a test whose fixture can drift from the shape the
   * service actually returns, which is the failure this whole migration was
   * about.
   *
   * `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is OFF here and on in src. In the service it
   * found a real defect. In a test, `rows[0].id` is written immediately after
   * the line that created `rows[0]`, and there are some nine hundred of them;
   * the flag would add nine hundred `?.` to code whose whole purpose is to
   * fail loudly when the thing it just made is not there.
   * ====================================================================== */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".",
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false
  },
  "include": ["test/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
